# The Filament toolchain pin: every artifact build (web today, tvOS / Android TV
# via the same sourced resolver) compiles against exactly this fork commit.
# Resolved by native/scripts/filament-checkout.sh; enforced at commit time by
# tests/native-artifact.test.js against the commit stamped in BUILD_STAMP.json.
#
# THE COMMIT MUST BE HELD BY A TAG on the fork, not merely by a branch. The
# branches this tree builds from are proposed upstream, so they get rebased and
# force-pushed, and the commit a branch used to point at then belongs to no ref:
# `git clone` stops fetching it and every fresh worktree and CI run fails to
# resolve the pin. A tag is fetched by a plain clone and never moves. The
# current one is `ttp-pin-2026-10-03` (upstream main + the tvOS PR branch + our
# emscripten build fix, which is NOT going upstream with it, + the Vulkan
# backend persisting its VkPipelineCache through the platform blob cache, + a
# bitset alignment fix without which upstream faults on 32-bit ARM; the last two
# are proposed upstream).
#
# TAGS ARE DATED, NEVER VERSIONED. The earlier `ttp-1.76.x` names read as
# Filament releases they were not: the patch set is the same few commits every
# time, and the only thing that moves is which upstream commit they sit on. A
# date says that; a version number invites someone to
# match it against a Filament release note.
#
# To upgrade Filament: tag the new fork commit and push the TAG, change
# FILAMENT_COMMIT, run native/scripts/build-runtime-web.sh, and commit pin +
# .filamat blobs + wasm TOGETHER — materials are MATERIAL_VERSION-locked to the
# tree, so a half upgrade fails at load time in the browser.
FILAMENT_REMOTE=https://github.com/tim4724/filament.git
FILAMENT_COMMIT=20c925cf9fd5068044234b8a39d6522c6342b1a4
